# 0100-not-supported-yet-guest-exit-warm-in-one-game-view.patch -- the owner's points X, Y and Z. Applies after 0099. With it, outside the patches: crates/ibuilder-pipeline src/state.rs
# (PreviousRun::GuestExit, last_exit_cause, classify_previous_run_exit, a test), crates/ibuilder-ffi (src/lib.rs ibuilder_classify_previous_run_exit, include/ibuilder.h
# IBUILDER_PREV_GUEST_EXIT 5, tests/c/test_abi.c). UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR: compiled, its pure part ran in the host harness, the Rust in cargo test (below).
#
# X. "Not supported yet". A build whose shader split found NO shader (the chain writes Documents/shaders/<id>.none and no shaders/<id>/b-<chain>.img: "the game will draw nothing until it
#    has a library") is said before the person plays it, read from those existing outputs (no new FFI), and, for a game with no engine table, profile-derived/<id>/game.tsv (the provisional
#    profile) adds "Its engine is not one iBuilder knows yet (a provisional profile).": "Not supported yet: iBuilder found no shader it can read in this game, so it will draw nothing (its
#    engine packs them in a format not handled yet). Logs help add it." On the grid card ("Not supported yet: no shader found"), the cover flow's and the iPad hero's note, the game's sheet
#    (a card at the top), the build screen's end (its line under the title) and the log ("[RED] build: <game>: …"), the notification ("Built, but not supported yet: no shader found"). Play
#    stays possible: the first time it asks "This game will draw nothing" with "Play anyway (sound and controls)" (remembered for this game), "Share the log", Cancel.
# Y. "The game closed itself". A boot that ended because the guest called svcExitProcess (the guest log's "[dm] received svcExitProcess: graceful exit"; its own output follows, so the cause is
#    read where it is: LastExitCause) is GuestExit (GameAppUi.ClassifyPreviousRun, the same rule as state.rs classify_previous_run_exit): not the player's Quit (the shim's "the player ended
#    the game" line wins), not the time limit, not a fault (a fatal signal's line), not a kill (a memory kill writes nothing: KilledOrUnknown). At the next launch: "<Game> closed itself after
#    N s (the game called exit). It may need a service iBuilder does not emulate yet; the log says which call came last." with "Share the log" and OK (titled "… right away" within 30 s);
#    N is the time from the boot's stage line (gameapp.stage's last write) to the guest log's last write: the guest log has no clock of its own. The log also gets the guest's last line before its
#    exit. No banner, no "interrupted", no resume offer: the marker is cleared as for the player's Quit.
# Z. The shader preparation in the Library's one-game view (the cover flow) and the iPad hero, as on the grid card: the live line and accent bar for the game being prepared (or the paused
#    queue's first), updated with the other views (UpdateWarmViews, its pace); "Shaders: <game> · waiting · 5,009" / "· paused" / "· skipped" (0098's words) for a built game in the queue;
#    nothing for a game with no preparation (WarmFlow.Of).
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-22, M1 Pro): check-patches-apply.sh: every patch 0010-0100 applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree. Compile
#   (-t:Compile, GameAppBuild.cs with FrameworkId as build-app.sh now writes it): 0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code as before 0080. Host harness (harness100: … P98;P100): 402
#   of 402 checks (15 new); 10 of 10 mutations killed. cargo test -p ibuilder-pipeline 267 passed (1 new: a guest exit vs the player's quit, a fault, the time limit, a kill, a run that never
#   booted), -p ibuilder-ffi 20 passed + c_abi 2 (test_abi.c: the new function and value); clippy -D warnings and fmt clean.
# NOT VERIFIED: nothing ran on a device: a real game that calls svcExitProcess, the alert at the next launch, a real .none build's warnings, the one-game view's bar.
# NEW UI STRINGS: Unsupported.Text, "Not supported yet: no shader found", " Its engine is not one iBuilder knows yet (a provisional profile).", "This game will draw nothing", "Play anyway (sound
#   and controls)", "Built, but not supported yet: no shader found", " closed itself", " (the game called exit). It may need a service iBuilder does not emulate yet; the log says which call
#   came last.", "The game closed itself", "The game closed itself right away", "Share the log", "Shaders: "; log lines "[RED] build: ", "the guest's last line before its exit: ".
